                  "category": null,
                  "details": [
                    "Listen and read develops students’ ability to connect spoken language with written text. It helps them build confidence in reading along with audio support."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Evidence of learning",
          "summary": null,
          "highlights": [],
          "contents": [
            {
              "section": null,
              "items": [
                {
                  "category": null,
                  "details": [
                    "Look for careful listening, accurate recognition of key vocabulary, and appropriate intonation when reading aloud."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Context",
          "summary": null,
          "highlights": [],
          "contents": [
            {
              "section": null,
              "items": [
                {
                  "category": null,
                  "details": [
                    "“How do you celebrate your birthday? Do you have a cake and candles? Let’s read about what children all around the world do and get some ideas for your next birthday.”"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Procedure",
          "summary": null,
          "highlights": [],
          "contents": [
            {
              "section": null,
              "items": [
                {
                  "category": null,
                  "details": [
                    "Heads Up (Reading): \nFocus the students’ attention on the CPT and help Ss to understand the text by asking questions, practicing skimming (reading for gist), scanning (reading for specific information) and detail (reading for comprehension). Then demonstrate the activity with TA/students.\nHeads Down: \nSs open their books. Instruct and ask ICQs. Then monitor, providing support and stretch where needed. Conduct activity feedback and error correction.\nHeads Together: \nDemo/Instruct and ask ICQs, including setting behaviour expectations. Then monitor, providing support and stretch where needed. Conduct activity feedback and error correction.\nReward moment\nCheck behaviour expectations and reward with APOS or remind for 4Rs"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "Student Book p.21 - B. Answer the questions",
      "timing": "15",
      "resourceId": null,
      "data": [
        {
          "title": "Stage aim",
          "summary": null,
          "highlights": [],
          "contents": [
            {
              "section": null,
              "items": [
                {
                  "category": null,
                  "details": [
                    "Answer the questions helps students show their understanding of the text or pictures by giving clear, simple answers. It supports reading comprehension, sentence building, and confidence using key vocabulary."
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
